{"content":[{"c":["HAZAR-ADDAR"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Town that, with Azmon, defined the southern border of Judah (",{"href":"?bref=Num.34.4","r":"Num.34.4","rawR":"Num.34.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.34.4","value":"Num.34.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nm 34:4"},"), usually identified with Khirbet el-Qudeirat near Kadesh-barnea. The parallel passage in ",{"href":"?bref=Josh.15.3-4","r":"Josh.15.3-4","rawR":"Josh.15.3-4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.15.3-4","value":"Josh.15.3-4"}],"t":"ref","v":"Joshua 15:3-4"}," lists four places—Hezron, Addar, Karka, and Azmon—instead of two. Some have suggested that Hazar-addar and Addar are the same place; others, that it was renamed Hezron to distinguish it from Addar."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"HazarAddar","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Nm 34:4","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.34.4","rawQueryValue":"Num.34.4","sourceRefExact":"Num.34.4"},{"anchorText":"Joshua 15:3-4","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.15.3-4","rawQueryValue":"Josh.15.3-4","sourceRefExact":"Josh.15.3-4"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"4fb20145696f8b9b9f0910129c076181743f4ced8148a167dfd335df49b157f9","sourceItemName":"HazarAddar","sourceItemOrder":172,"sourceMember":"Articles/H.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"HazarAddar","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Hazar-Addar","title":"Hazar-Addar","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}